  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_283_1d4_o1`, using 4 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_283_1d4_o1.lean`):\n- **Subject and trigger:** the subject is in the pedestrian aggregate. The rule applies when some pedestrian head shows `dont_walk_steady`, governs a roadway or lane `r`, the subject faces it, and the subject was not on `r` at the previous observation. \"Faces\" uses the record's own inequalities, squared so there is no division or square root.\n- **Previous observation:** Core has no operator for \"at the previous observation\", so I wrote it with `rises` only: `rises(occ) ∨ (¬occ ∧ ¬rises(¬occ))`. When both values are known, this means exactly \"was not on `r` before\".\n- **Exception for a crossing already under way:** `since(not on a sidewalk, lawful entry)`. A lawful entry is stepping off a sidewalk onto a roadway or lane whose head shows `walk`, or flashing don't-walk with a countdown, while facing that head.\n- **The nine composed rules** are each written as \"does not apply\"; the two whose subject is a vehicle are checked under \"some road user `v`\".\n- **Obligation:** it repeats the whole selection of head and region and requires that the subject is not on `r` now.\n- **Narrowings:** none. The two choices above change how the record is written, not what it means.\n\n**Witnesses:** the five planned ones, plus two I added so the lane cases are exercised:\n- `branch_2` (violated): stepping into a lane while its head shows steady don't-walk.\n- `branch_3` (not applicable): a crossing begun under `walk` onto a lane.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **`UNUSED_CLAIM`:** I ran the gate on the untouched skeleton by mistake.\n2. **`UNCLAIMED_ATOM st_travel_region`:** the gate counts a quantifier's region kind as a claimed atom. I switched to separate `roadway` and `lane` quantifiers.\n3. **`WITNESS_FAIL`:** one of the composed rules reads the lane direction of the roadway being crossed, and my scenes didn't set it. I gave the roadway a direction and added a marked crosswalk over the crossing.\n4. **`OK`.**\n\nOne extra shell command (`gate --help`) was blocked by the permission system and did not run. It didn't use up a gate run. I found nothing wrong with the node itself.\n\nFiles are in `.../iter-005/code/NRS_484B_283_1d4_o1/`:\n- `task_result.md`",
